Phase 3B.2 (in-progress) AppGL patch to SPIRV-Cross for TES-as-compute.
The ragged diff form is intentional — each hunk is a self-contained
feature so a rebase onto a different upstream SHA can merge pieces
independently. See specs-worker-docs/phase3b-tf-capture-design.md for
the full rationale.

INCOMPLETE: the kernel MSL produced by this patch is well-formed but
references undeclared `gl_TessCoord` and `gl_PrimitiveID` locals. The
remaining 3B.2.4 work adds a new entry-point-arg
`spvDomainData [[buffer(25)]]` + a `fixup_hooks_in` hook that seeds
those locals from the buffer before the body runs. Until that
lands, the kernel won't pass `newLibraryWithSource` — but the MSL
string is stashed only, not compiled; this patch is regression-free.

--- a/spirv_msl.hpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.hpp
@@ -429,6 +429,28 @@ public:
 		// to index the output buffer.
 		bool vertex_for_tessellation = false;

+		// AppGL fork addition (phase-3B-metal-tess-TF): when set, a
+		// tessellation evaluation shader is translated as a compute
+		// kernel rather than a `[[patch(...)]] vertex` function.
+		// Used by the AppGL transform-feedback capture path, which
+		// dispatches one TES kernel thread per tessellator-generated
+		// vertex (the caller supplies the domain coords in a buffer;
+		// the kernel writes per-vertex TF output into a user-bound
+		// buffer). Companion to `vertex_for_tessellation` but for
+		// the post-tessellator stage.
+		//
+		// Requires `raw_buffer_tese_input = true` so gl_in / per-patch
+		// inputs already live in buffers (buffer slots 22 / 20).
+		// Output is written through a new TF-capture struct at
+		// `shader_output_buffer_index` (buffer 28 by default).
+		//
+		// Orthogonal to isoline-tessellation support, which Metal
+		// does not implement natively — the compute form still
+		// throws on isolines. Domain-point generation for isolines
+		// happens on the AppGL side.
+		bool tess_evaluation_as_compute = false;
+
 		// Assume that SubpassData images have multiple layers. Layered input attachments
 		// are addressed relative to the Layer output from the vertex pipeline. This option
 		// has no effect with multiview, since all input attachments are assumed to be layered

--- a/spirv_msl.cpp   (build_implicit_builtins: extend `need_grid_params`)
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -269,1 +269,6 @@
-	bool need_grid_params = get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelVertex && msl_options.vertex_for_tessellation;
+	// AppGL patch (phase-3B-metal-tess-TF): TES-as-compute also needs the
+	// grid-params synthesis so `builtin_invocation_id_id` gets a valid
+	// BuiltInGlobalInvocationId variable — the output index
+	// `spvOut[gl_GlobalInvocationID.x]` depends on this.
+	bool need_grid_params = (get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelVertex && msl_options.vertex_for_tessellation) ||
+	                         (get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelTessellationEvaluation && msl_options.tess_evaluation_as_compute);

